<title>AUSTRALIA: Australia's AWB says sells no wheat in tender 24.</title>
<headline>Australia's AWB says sells no wheat in tender 24.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Australian Wheat Board (AWB) said on Wednesday it sold no wheat in its latest tender for sales from its national pool.</p>
<p>Total bids were received for 30,000 tonnes of current crop wheat and for 6,000 tonnes of 1997/98 season wheat, it said.</p>
<p>Highest failed bids A$/tonne:</p>
<p>    Port zone   Grade   Current crop   New crop</p>
<p>    Newcastle   APH     212.00</p>
<p>		    AH1     197.00</p>
<p>		    ASW     191.00	   167.50</p>
<p>    Port Kembla APH     212.50</p>
<p>		    AH1     198.00</p>
<p>		    ASW     192.00</p>
<p>    Geelong     ASW     189.00</p>
<p>    Fremantle   ASW     202.00</p>
<p>AWB Reserve Tender Price</p>
<p>    Port Zone   Grade   Current crop   New crop</p>
<p>    Newcastle   ASW     202.00	   195.00</p>
<p>    Port Kembla ASW     202.00	   195.00</p>
<p>    Geelong     ASW     200.00	   193.00</p>
<p>    Freemantle  ASW     207.00	   200.00</p>
<p>The next tender would be held on June 11, the AWB said.</p>
<p>Note: ASW = Australian Standard White; APH = Australian Prime Hard; AH1 = Australian Hard 1; APW = Australian Premium White.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
